WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.062
Lokalise exports your
keys as resource files,

2
00:00:04.062 --> 00:00:07.254
and you keep those files and
their reviewed translations.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.657
General Translation
imports those files,

4
00:00:10.657 --> 00:00:13.326
then translates new
and changed strings.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.494
Export with lokalise2 file download,

6
00:00:17.494 --> 00:00:20.014
and set empty translations to skip,

7
00:00:20.014 --> 00:00:21.557
so gaps are not imported.

8
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.624
Then delete the auto-pull webhook,

9
00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.029
stop the GitHub trigger,

10
00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:28.408
and remove Lokalise's
GitHub Actions.

11
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.424
List the files in gt.config.json,

12
00:00:32.424 --> 00:00:36.533
import your glossary, and add key
descriptions as per-key context.

13
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:42.618
Run npx gt upload before
the first npx gt translate,

14
00:00:42.618 --> 00:00:45.392
so exported translations
are not overwritten.

15
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.587
Your team now ships
French with each release.
